  "description": "The 2026 Wyoming gubernatorial election is an open-seat race to elect the next governor of Wyoming, as incumbent Republican Governor Mark Gordon is term-limited and cannot seek re-election. Four Republicans (Brent Bien, Curt Blake, Eric Barlow, and Megan Degenfelder) are competing in the August 18 Republican primary, while Kenneth Casner is the sole Democratic candidate. Wyoming is a deeply Republican state, making the Republican primary the most competitive stage of this contest, with candidates focused on energy policy, education, and state sovereignty. The general election is expected to favor the Republican nominee in this reliably red state.",
